ผู้ใช้ + ขอบเขต (in/out)
ตัววัดความสำเร็จ (success metrics)

* **Problem**
	Researchers and reviewers experience significant delays, manual verification errors, and lack of tracking visibility during research grant applicatoins due to paper-based submission and 
repetitive data entry.

* **Users**
	- Researchers 
	- School Deans/Chairs
	- School Secretaries
	- Research Operations/Finance Staff

* **Scope**
	
	| IN SCOPE (MVP this term) | OUT OF SCOPE (explicit promise) |
| :--- | :--- |
| **FR-1** Manage grant call cycles, deadlines, and tier caps. | Contract signing and project bank account recording. |
| **FR-2** Single-source Researcher Profile & RS-01 .docx import. | Installment tracking and disbursement payouts (50/40/10). |
| **FR-3** Budget Form 17.2 (Excel/Web) with tier & 25% sub-cap validation. | Progress report submissions and final full report evaluation. |
| **FR-4** School-level Endorsement & Secretary tracking dashboard. | Financial voucher auditing (WJ.1–9) and asset return. |
| **FR-5** Parallel 2-Track Review (Content/Finance) & Auto-Route Revise Loop. | Post-award change requests (time extensions, budget transfers). |
| **FR-6** Executive Committee resolutions & Award Announcement generation. | 100-point rubric scoring (deprecated for Comment-based in Phase 1). |

* **Success Metrics**
	| No. | SuccessMetric | Testing method |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1** | Users can track the status of project proposals. | Change the proposal status and verify that the dashboard displays the correct status. |
| **2** | The system correctly handles proposal endorsement and returns proposals for revision. | Test the endorsement, return-for-revision, and resubmission processes. |
| **3** | The system locks approved information and routes proposals back to the correct reviewers.| Approve one review track, return the proposal for revision, and verify that the approved infomation remains locked and the proposal is routed to the correct reviewers.|
